WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.839
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Daniel. Welcome to Online Upper-Intermediate.

2
00:00:05.139 --> 00:00:08.456
Hi! I'm Nita. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.756 --> 00:00:15.878
Unit twenty: Social Responsibility. In this unit, you will discuss how businesses and people help society.

4
00:00:16.883 --> 00:00:18.929
corporate social responsibility.

5
00:00:19.629 --> 00:00:24.740
corporate social responsibility means a company's duty to help society and the environment.

6
00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:28.909
The bank's corporate social responsibility programme builds schools.

7
00:00:29.609 --> 00:00:32.819
Your turn. Say: corporate social responsibility.

8
00:00:35.519 --> 00:00:37.576
corporate social responsibility.

9
00:00:38.583 --> 00:00:39.515
philanthropy.

10
00:00:40.215 --> 00:00:43.433
philanthropy means giving money and time to help other people.

11
00:00:43.733 --> 00:00:46.279
His philanthropy funded three hospitals.

12
00:00:46.979 --> 00:00:49.329
Your turn. Say: philanthropy.

13
00:00:52.029 --> 00:00:53.077
philanthropy.

14
00:00:54.083 --> 00:00:55.526
social enterprise.

15
00:00:56.226 --> 00:01:00.477
social enterprise means a business whose main goal is to help society.

16
00:01:00.777 --> 00:01:03.950
The café is a social enterprise that trains young people.

17
00:01:04.650 --> 00:01:07.360
Your turn. Say: social enterprise.

18
00:01:10.060 --> 00:01:11.549
social enterprise.

19
00:01:12.550 --> 00:01:13.470
fair trade.

20
00:01:14.170 --> 00:01:17.470
fair trade means trade that pays producers a fair price.

21
00:01:17.770 --> 00:01:20.582
This coffee is fair trade, so farmers earn more.

22
00:01:21.282 --> 00:01:24.166
Your turn. Say: fair trade.

23
00:01:26.866 --> 00:01:27.844
fair trade.

24
00:01:28.850 --> 00:01:30.107
ethical business.

25
00:01:30.807 --> 00:01:34.466
ethical business means a company that acts honestly and responsibly.

26
00:01:34.766 --> 00:01:37.671
Customers prefer to buy from an ethical business.

27
00:01:38.371 --> 00:01:41.128
Your turn. Say: ethical business.

28
00:01:43.828 --> 00:01:45.201
ethical business.

29
00:01:46.217 --> 00:01:47.253
volunteerism.

30
00:01:47.953 --> 00:01:51.612
volunteerism means the practice of doing unpaid work to help others.

31
00:01:51.912 --> 00:01:54.922
Volunteerism is growing among Cambodian students.

32
00:01:55.622 --> 00:01:57.845
Your turn. Say: volunteerism.

33
00:02:00.545 --> 00:02:01.662
volunteerism.

34
00:02:02.650 --> 00:02:03.779
charity work.

35
00:02:04.479 --> 00:02:07.523
charity work means work done to help people in need.

36
00:02:07.823 --> 00:02:10.392
She does charity work at an orphanage on weekends.

37
00:02:11.092 --> 00:02:13.674
Your turn. Say: charity work.

38
00:02:16.374 --> 00:02:17.538
charity work.

39
00:02:18.550 --> 00:02:19.888
community outreach.

40
00:02:20.588 --> 00:02:24.526
community outreach means programmes that bring services to local people.

41
00:02:24.826 --> 00:02:28.010
The hospital's community outreach team visits villages.

42
00:02:28.710 --> 00:02:31.594
Your turn. Say: community outreach.

43
00:02:34.294 --> 00:02:35.772
community outreach.

44
00:02:36.783 --> 00:02:38.678
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:38.978 --> 00:02:42.696
I'm considering working for a social enterprise after graduation.

46
00:02:43.983 --> 00:02:46.659
That's admirable. Do you mind telling me why?

47
00:02:47.950 --> 00:02:52.146
I'd like to avoid working only for profit. I want to make a difference.

48
00:02:53.450 --> 00:02:57.156
Many companies now invest in corporate social responsibility too.

49
00:02:58.450 --> 00:03:03.050
True, but I prefer helping directly, like through community outreach.

50
00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:07.441
Then you might enjoy combining a job with some charity work.

51
00:03:08.750 --> 00:03:12.549
Grammar focus: Gerunds and infinitives (advanced).

52
00:03:12.849 --> 00:03:15.046
Some verbs change meaning with -ing or to.

53
00:03:15.346 --> 00:03:20.585
Remember plus -ing is about a past memory; remember plus to is about something you must do.

54
00:03:20.885 --> 00:03:25.952
For example: I remember volunteering at the orphanage. Remember to donate before Friday.

55
00:03:26.252 --> 00:03:30.701
Some verbs change meaning depending on whether they are followed by -ing or to + verb.

56
00:03:31.717 --> 00:03:34.427
Now read and listen. Business with a Purpose.

57
00:03:34.727 --> 00:03:37.760
More and more young people want to work for an ethical business.

58
00:03:39.050 --> 00:03:43.070
Social enterprises try to make a profit while solving social problems.

59
00:03:44.383 --> 00:03:49.065
Many large companies have stopped seeing corporate social responsibility as just marketing.

60
00:03:50.350 --> 00:03:54.161
Fair trade products help farmers earn enough to send their children to school.

61
00:03:55.450 --> 00:03:59.121
Philanthropy and volunteerism remind us that everyone can contribute.

62
00:04:00.417 --> 00:04:02.756
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

63
00:04:03.056 --> 00:04:05.833
Trade that pays producers a fair price is blank.

64
00:04:06.133 --> 00:04:10.019
A, fair trade. B, philanthropy. C, volunteerism.

65
00:04:14.017 --> 00:04:16.039
The answer is A: fair trade.

66
00:04:17.550 --> 00:04:19.805
Please remember blank the door when you leave.

67
00:04:20.105 --> 00:04:22.957
A, locking. B, to lock. C, lock.

68
00:04:26.950 --> 00:04:29.019
The answer is B: to lock.

69
00:04:30.517 --> 00:04:33.433
I'll never forget blank the Angkor sunrise for the first time.

70
00:04:33.733 --> 00:04:36.760
A, seeing. B, to see. C, see.

71
00:04:40.750 --> 00:04:42.657
The answer is A: seeing.

72
00:04:44.150 --> 00:04:47.427
A business whose main goal is to help society is a blank.

73
00:04:47.727 --> 00:04:52.344
A, social enterprise. B, community outreach. C, charity work.

74
00:04:56.350 --> 00:04:58.733
The answer is A: social enterprise.

75
00:05:00.217 --> 00:05:03.389
According to the text, fair trade helps farmers to blank.

76
00:05:03.689 --> 00:05:08.167
A, buy cars. B, send their children to school. C, travel abroad.

77
00:05:12.150 --> 00:05:14.962
The answer is B: send their children to school.

78
00:05:16.450 --> 00:05:20.774
Now it's your turn to speak. Should companies be responsible for helping society?

79
00:05:26.074 --> 00:05:33.463
Yes. I'd like companies to stop focusing only on profit and start investing in education and the environment.

80
00:05:33.763 --> 00:05:35.206
Excellent answer, Nita!

81
00:05:36.217 --> 00:05:40.552
Great work today! You learned eight new words and gerunds and infinitives (advanced).

82
00:05:40.852 --> 00:05:44.143
Today's value is community. Help the people in your town.

83
00:05:44.443 --> 00:05:46.980
See you in Unit twenty-one. Goodbye!

84
00:05:47.280 --> 00:05:49.862
Thank you, Mr. Daniel! Bye, everyone!

